{
  "description": "Commitment vectors (spec/protocols/mcp-terms-extension.md, check 5, and spec/protocols/terms-receipt.md, check 7). Each vector is terms, the scope of a request, and an operator's tolerance. Terms with several rules pin which rule governs: the first rule for the scope itself in the terms' own order, or failing that the first for the nearest scope above it. A vector has either the commitment the operator signs when it serves the request, or the refusal it gives. A served vector also lists overclaims: conditions that claim more than the rule gave, each of which the agent refuses in a receipt, as it accepts the commitment.",
